{"key":"i10-s0194","rationale":"Idea:\nThe primary motivation for this architectural evolution is to further enhance the ","callouts":{"1":"Spiking short convolutions: each q/k/v/g current is first turned into spikes by a LIF neuron, so the causal depthwise convolution runs on binary spike trains.","2":"Binary write / keep: LIF neurons on β = ½σ(·) and γ = σ(w) make the write strength and decay {0, 1} per head and token, so a token either writes its delta error or not, and the state is kept in proportion to the fraction of 'keep' spikes in the chunk.","3":"Spike output gate: the normalised read-out is multiplied by binary spikes of a LIF neuron on the gate branch (the expert uses SiLU), hard-masking channels.","4":"Spiking residual gates: a d → d spiking projection of the residual stream drives a LIF neuron whose binary spikes switch each channel of the sub-layer output on or off before the add."},"notes":[{"text":"rate loss computed, unused","kind":"evolved"}],"meta":"Iteration 10 · sample 194  ·  DeltaProduct state update  ·  unstable run","nodes":{"n1":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L306","tip":null},"gp":{"label":"g proj","code":"L175","tip":null},"q":{"label":"q proj","code":"L170","tip":null},"k":{"label":"k proj","code":"L171","tip":null},"v":{"label":"v proj","code":"L172","tip":null},"bp":{"label":"β proj","code":"L173","tip":null},"wp":{"label":"w proj","code":"L174","tip":null},"cg":{"label":"SpkConv₄","code":"L184","tip":null,"novel":1},"cq":{"label":"SpkConv₄","code":"L181","tip":null,"novel":1},"ck":{"label":"SpkConv₄","code":"L182","tip":null,"novel":1},"cv":{"label":"SpkConv₄","code":"L183","tip":null,"novel":1},"bs":{"label":"½σ","code":"L195","tip":null},"ws":{"label":"σ","code":"L196","tip":null},"lb":{"label":"LIF","code":"L199","tip":null,"novel":2},"lw":{"label":"LIF","code":"L200","tip":null,"novel":2},"lg":{"label":"LIF","code":"L205","tip":null,"novel":3},"core":{"label":"Gated delta","code":"L38-L100","tip":null},"onorm":{"label":"RMSNorm","cod